      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The classic rule is that a home should cost roughly three times your gross annual income.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "home",
          "big": "~3×",
          "label": "income to home price",
          "props": [
            "home",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Lenders judge you on your debt-to-income ratio.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-dti",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · debt-to-income"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So a sixty thousand dollar salary safely supports a house around two hundred thousand, not far more.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "home",
          "big": "$205K",
          "label": "the house a $60K salary affords",
          "props": [
            "home",
            "check"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A mortgage stretches that price over decades of monthly payments.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-mortgage",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · mortgage loan"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Push past that, and the monthly payment quietly eats your whole life.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "red",
          "line": "It eats your life",
          "props": [
            "home",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The amortization schedule shows how little early payments touch the balance.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-amort",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · amortization"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The market, though, often prices homes at five to six times income, which is the real squeeze.",
      "shots": [
